{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Instances.RealVectorSpace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.phi_splits_channels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.phi_splits_channels","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L272-L283","doc":"**The `Δ`-weighted functional splits the projector channels, in both readings, with the\nbound channel swapped between them.** With positive Markov weights:\ndirect reading — `T = 1` positive, `T = 0` negative; difference reading — `T = 1` negative,\n`T = 0` positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.phi_one_sub_Pminus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.phi_one_sub_Pminus","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L263-L268","doc":"Difference reading, `T = 0`: `Φ(1) − Φ(P₋) = y_(2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.phi_one_sub_Pplus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.phi_one_sub_Pplus","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L256-L261","doc":"Difference reading, `T = 1`: `Φ(1) − Φ(P₊) = −y_(1,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.phi_Pminus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.phi_Pminus","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L249-L254","doc":"`Φ(P₋) = −y_(1,1)`, `P₋ = s(q − σ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.phi_Pplus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.phi_Pplus","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L242-L247","doc":"`Φ(P₊) = y_(2)`, `P₊ = s(σ + q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.phi","kind":"def","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L239-L240","doc":"`Φ = Σ_λ y_λ χ^λ Δ_λ` at `n = 2`, with `Δ_(2) = +1`, `Δ_(1,1) = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.chiAlt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.chiAlt","kind":"def","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L236-L237","doc":"`χ^(1,1)` on `a·1 + b·σ` (σ acts by `−q⁻¹` on the antisymmetric block). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.chiSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.chiSym","kind":"def","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L233-L234","doc":"`χ^(2)` on `a·1 + b·σ` (σ acts by `q` on the symmetric block). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.mayer_projector_both_bind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.mayer_projector_both_bind","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L221-L225","doc":"Same for the Mayer two-body law. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.negLog_projector_both_bind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.negLog_projector_both_bind","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L214-L219","doc":"**Concrete instance.** Under the projector decomposition the log law binds both channels,\nfor every positive scale. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.mayer_strictAntiOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.mayer_strictAntiOn","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L207-L212","doc":"The Mayer two-body law `B = c(1 − μ)`, `c > 0`, is in the class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.negLog_strictAntiOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.negLog_strictAntiOn","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L199-L205","doc":"The log law `B = −c · ln μ`, `c > 0`, is in the class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.projector_channels_same_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.projector_channels_same_sign","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L186-L195","doc":"**No law of the ratio alone splits the projector channels.** For `F` strictly monotone\nin either direction with `F 1 = 0`, the two channels have the same sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.projector_channels_both_unbound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.projector_channels_both_unbound","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L177-L184","doc":"Reversing the trace→energy direction (an increasing law) unbinds both channels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.projector_channels_both_bind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.projector_channels_both_bind","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L171-L175","doc":"**Under the projector decomposition every decreasing law binds both channels.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.lt_iff_gt_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.lt_iff_gt_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L165-L169","doc":"**The ordering is the law's business only through `μ`.** Channel `1` binds less than\nchannel `2` iff its ratio is larger — for every strictly decreasing law. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.neg_iff_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.neg_iff_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L150-L163","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.pos_iff_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.pos_iff_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L133-L148","doc":"The sign of the binding is the sign of `1 − μ`, for every strictly decreasing law\nvanishing at the free point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.cauchy_admits_every_constant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.cauchy_admits_every_constant","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L116-L125","doc":"**Additivity does not fix the constant.** Every `c · log`, for every real `c`, satisfies\nboth hypotheses — so the sign (trace→energy direction) and the scale stay free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.eq_mul_log_of_logAdditive_of_continuousOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.eq_mul_log_of_logAdditive_of_continuousOn","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L95-L114","doc":"**Additivity + continuity force the logarithm.** Any continuous solution of\n`f (x*y) = f x + f y` on `(0, ∞)` is `c · log` with `c = f e`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.map_one_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.map_one_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L90-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.IsLogAdditiveOnPos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingLawClassInvariants.IsLogAdditiveOnPos","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingLawClassInvariants.lean#L86-L88","doc":"The multiplicative-to-additive property on the positive reals. ","signatureChunk":0}]}